  "description": "XUHWAA crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C119 H93 Ce3 Mn7 O46,6(C1 H3 N1 O2). From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 10 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce3 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn3 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn4 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn5 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn6 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn7 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 21 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 2.957-3.918 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 80.36-141.71°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Ce3IVMn7IIIO8(O2CPh)17(H2O)4]·6MeNO2. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
